==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cat Gang''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Heavy Assault C.A.T.''' when obtained from [[Box Cats Awaken!|Box Cat Awaken!]] (may drop on the first stage but guaranteed on the second) and is at level 20.

==Strategy/Usage==
The Cats in a Box are a helpful unit earlier on, as they share a similar niche to [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cat]] by delivering a burst of damage to the frontlines. This unit isn't a replacement for a [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rusher]] like [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cat]]: it's instead a unit to get in when the enemy is idle. Unfortunately, they become underwhelming because of their massively underpowered stats beyond [[Empire of Cats]]. As a result, [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cow Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] are much better alternatives.

==='''True Form'''===
By the time Heavy Assault C.A.T. is unlocked, their stats have long fallen behind, making them completely useless. Their weaken ability doesn't do much to falter [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies as a whole since it can't kill them outright, nor stall them as well as [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] can. Serious use should only be considered if [[Talents]] are factored in.

==='''Talents'''===
Through their '''[[Massive Damage]]''' and '''Attack Buff''' Talents, this unit becomes much more powerful. Their damage is increased by more than seven times, turning this unit from a weak debuffer to something closer to a mini-[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Yukimura]]. Their low range incentivizes deploying them to rush bosses and other similarly strong units, because they otherwise struggle against peons in a way which other anti-Dark units like [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] do not. Their speed allows them to get in safely and deal massive damage, albeit requiring some timing due to their aforementioned low range. For this reason, enemies like [[Masked Okame]] and [[Le'noir]] are great matchups. Even as a generalist rusher, Heavy Assault C.A.T. can be a solid choice due to their cooldown and slightly above-average range.

'''HP Buff''' is as important as for any rusher, because even a slight health increase can allow them to land one more valuable hit.

'''Resist Slow''' can be safely ignored, as Dark enemies rely mostly on brute force and little on special abilities. They are only helpful in mixed stages, where it would be wiser to spend the NP elsewhere anyway.

'''Weaken Immune''' is similarly niche. While it does make [[Dark Dober]] and [[Crocodylidae Kurocroc]] a more favorable matchup toward the lategame, consider your other options by the time these enemies make their debuts.

==='''Orb'''===
A Dark Massive Damage Up Orb is the only sensible choice, since players who invest in its talents will most likely purchase the Massive Damage Talent.

